From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dean Marx via kernel-team <kernel-team@lists.ubuntu.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:21:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UBUNTU: SAUCE: integrity: Load MokListRT certs into the
 machine keyring

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2131181

The MokListRT path was refactored to share parsing with MokListXRT.
Before the refactor, MokListRT used get_handler_for_mok(). The refactored
code instead defaults to get_handler_for_db(), which is the handler for
the firmware db and routes certificates to the .platform keyring.

As a result, certificates enrolled through mokutil and MokManager are
loaded into the .platform keyring rather than the .machine keyring. MOK
certificates are intended to be handled as Machine Owner Keys, distinct
from platform certificates originating from the firmware db and KEK.

Restore get_handler_for_mok() as the default handler for MokListRT. The
MokListXRT path continues to select get_handler_for_dbx(), retaining the
EFI MOKvar config table support added for large revocation lists. This
targeted correction avoids reverting that support, which is needed when
a large MokListXRT is split across MokListXRT1, MokListXRT2, and
MokListXRT3.

Fixes: 0ba9d5044222 ("UBUNTU: SAUCE: integrity: Load mokx certs from the EFI MOK config table")
Signed-off-by: Dean Marx <dean.marx@canonical.com>
Acked-by: Stefan Bader <stefan.bader@canonical.com>
Acked-by: Chia-Lin Kao <acelan.kao@canonical.com>
Signed-off-by: Stefan Bader <stefan.bader@canonical.com>
Ledger-Change: C-00386
Ledger-Origin: ubuntu@71a4cad30e47c5bb0018f8d961e8e19dd06c8951
---
 security/integrity/platform_certs/load_uefi.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/security/integrity/platform_certs/load_uefi.c b/security/integrity/platform_certs/load_uefi.c
index facdaa983a46..3f4a75160f60 100644
--- a/security/integrity/platform_certs/load_uefi.c
+++ b/security/integrity/platform_certs/load_uefi.c
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@ static int __init load_moklist_certs(const bool load_db)
 	efi_char16_t *efivar_name = L"MokListRT";
 	const char *parse_mokvar_name = "UEFI:MokListRT (MOKvar table)";
 	const char *parse_efivar_name = "UEFI:MokListRT";
-	efi_element_handler_t (*get_handler_for_guid)(const efi_guid_t *) = get_handler_for_db;
+	efi_element_handler_t (*get_handler_for_guid)(const efi_guid_t *) = get_handler_for_mok;
 
 	if (!load_db) {
 		mokvar_name = "MokListXRT";
